cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  KyberSlash Reproducibility and Mitigation Evaluation Harness
message: >-
  If you use this software or its data, please cite both the software and
  the dissertation it supports.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Mateen"
    family-names: "Rafique"
    affiliation: Manchester Metropolitan University
abstract: >-
  An evaluation harness that builds pinned ML-KEM and Kyber revisions across a
  compiler and optimisation matrix, gates on functional correctness, and audits
  each binary for secret-dependent variable-latency division with per-function
  attribution. Includes a divider-model instrumented timing harness for measuring
  operand-level leakage on hosts whose divider is constant-latency.
keywords:
  - ML-KEM
  - Kyber
  - KyberSlash
  - timing side channel
  - constant-time
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ace7111/kyberslash-evaluation"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
references:
